module gunbc.source_integration_landing_spine


data source_integration_landing_spine_note: std.types.NonEmptyStr = "P0 landing spine. Full P−1 claims and admitted evidence flow into one readiness receipt; the proposal guarantee population is the readiness policy population by construction. Support-only, challenge-only, conflict, missing evidence, admission refusal, and duplicate requirements remain distinct. One closed-space receipt owns ready evidence, admission contract, equivalence, candidate population, and seven semantic closure axes; zero, one, and many are projections of that receipt, never caller labels. Admission nests the exact closed-one receipt. A transition nests the exact admission, independent read-back nests that transition, and each compatibility projection names the same accepted transition through a typed semantic-to-native target binding. Only a matched read-back can project Landed. Normative options own their material result or proposal amendment, and the selected structural position remains in the resume identity; a free token is only a transport hint. Audience-projected text is distinct from internal cause and locus. The terminal surface is exactly Landed | ChoiceRequired | CouldNotLand; unfinished work is a separate machine-owned arm. Commit freshness is a transition-time exact-parent precondition, not an early semantic closure certificate. This is P0 construction, not the P1 proof kernel, P2 capture, P3 effect transport, or a CLI."

